  "family": "doubleboxBlockmass",
  "source": "Doublebox 2L 4-leg with BLOCK 2-mass pattern (mAsq on l1's two rails — propagators 0 and 1; mBsq on l2's two rails — propagators 3 and 5).  Direct topological complement to doublebox2m (D12 regression guard, which has the same family with INTERLEAVED cross-loop mass placement).  Same kinematics as doublebox_sv / doublebox2m: s=-3, t=-1, mAsq=1, mBsq=4 (Euclidean).  Unlike the interleaved D12 case which needed elevated precision, this block placement converges at default (working_pre=120, x_order=240, extra_x_order=280) — confirming the audit's argument that the precision sensitivity is interleaved-specific, driven by the complex pole pair η²+η+12 that arises only when the η-injected propagators sit in different loops with the same mass.",
